    "body": "@annevk resetting does not solve the issue and will still be inconsistent.\n\nThe only consistent behavior that I could think of that allows combining `fatal: true` and `stream: true` is setting an `errored` flag and continuing throwing on any input until a final non-stream `decode()` clears the flag (and also throws one final time).\n\nThat way, no misdecoded data will produced, and the streamed output will always match a non-fatal prefix.\n\nE.g. resetting an `ISO-2022-JP` decoder to ASCII and mismatching non-replaced data between replacement and fatal, or mismatching non-replaced utf-16 data between replacement and fatal could pose security risks.\n\nWith auto-resets, both `ISO-2022-JP` and `UTF-16` could be tricked into outputting html code after a reset even when a replacement-decoded text does not contain any html syntax.\n\n`ISO-2022-JP` could be tricked into that without resets, too.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
